      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Libertarianism fundamentally fails because it ignores the reality that a free market cannot function without a baseline of social order, which requires government enforcement of laws against crime and fraud. Their insistence on absolute deregulation would collapse essential public services like healthcare, education, and infrastructure, leaving the vulnerable with no safety net. Furthermore, their anti-tax stance is logically inconsistent with their support for a massive military-industrial complex, as the defense budget is far larger than any proposed tax cut would ever be. Ultimately, their platform prioritizes abstract economic theories over the tangible needs of working families, making them an unreliable partner for any serious national strategy.",
